msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:231
msgid "**Blynk account and libraries**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:233
msgid "The first three lines say which Blynk device this board belongs to. They come from the device page and are identical in every project of this kit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:247
msgid "**The serial port that talks to the module**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:249
msgid "The ESPC2-01 works as a modem: the sketch sends it AT commands. On the R4 it is wired to D0/D1, which is ``Serial1``, a hardware port, so 115200 works without bit errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:258
msgid "The function ``espModuleInit()`` waits for the module to finish booting and then sends ``ATE0`` to switch the echo off. Without it the module's start-up log and the echoed commands end up mixed with the replies, and Blynk cannot read them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:262
msgid "**The DHT11 sensor**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:274
msgid "A DHT11 returns whole degrees and whole percent, so a ``float`` is more precision than the sensor really has - but it keeps the code simple and the same for a DHT22 later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:277
msgid "**The soil moisture sensor and the two thresholds**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:288
msgid "The probe returns an analogue value between 0 and 1023, and **the wetter the soil, the lower the number**. That is why the sketch says \"below ``wetSoil`` = too wet\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:293
msgid "Measure the two numbers yourself. Push the probe into a glass of water and read the value: that is roughly your ``wetSoil``. Then read it in dry soil: that is ``drySoil``. The defaults 320 / 400 only fit the soil of the developer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:297
msgid "**setup()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:315
msgid "``timer.setInterval(5000L, myTimerEvent)`` measures once every five seconds. A DHT11 cannot do better than one reading per second anyway, and plants do not change faster than that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:319
msgid "**loop()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:328
msgid "``Blynk.run()`` keeps the connection alive, ``timer.run()`` fires the measurement. Nothing here may block, or the cloud drops the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:331
msgid "**sendData() - measure, judge, report**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:365
msgid "``return`` on a failed DHT reading leaves the dashboard showing the last good value instead of overwriting it with ``nan``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:367
msgid "``Blynk.virtualWrite(V3, ...)`` and friends push the four values to the datastreams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:368
msgid "``Blynk.virtualWrite(V6, 255)`` turns the **LED widget on the dashboard** fully on; ``Blynk.setProperty(V6, \"color\", color)`` then paints it green or red. The real LED marked **L** on the board is not used by this project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:372
msgid "**printData()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/03-iot_Plant_monitor.rst:388
msgid "The same numbers, but on the Serial Monitor. When something looks wrong on the phone, this is where you check whether the sensor or the cloud is to blame."
msgstr ""
